// A speaker is written `name (a, b):`, with one space before the values, a comma and a space between them, and none inside the parentheses. With a full-width colon it is `name（a、b）：`, with no spaces.

@channel pose
@channel effect: still, shake
@actor mira
    name: Mira
    pose: neutral, happy

== kitchen.door
mira(happy): This line has no space before the values.
// PIB5033
mira ( happy ): This line has spaces inside the parentheses.
// PIB5033
mira (happy,shake): This line has no space after the comma.
// PIB5033
mira : This line has a space before the colon.
// PIB5033
mira （happy 、shake）：This line has spaces around full-width punctuation.
// PIB5033
mira（happy）: This line has an ASCII colon, which makes the usual form ASCII.
// PIB5033

// Must not trigger

mira (happy): This line uses the usual spacing.
mira (happy, shake): So does this one, with two values.
mira: So does this one.
mira（happy、shake）：This line uses the usual full-width spacing.
mira：So does this one.
